WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.720 --> 00:00:03.480
- For most of my life, I was told that

00:00:03.480 --> 00:00:05.531
I was never going to be
able to throw a curveball,

00:00:05.531 --> 00:00:08.851
let alone pitch, because of my condition.

00:00:08.851 --> 00:00:13.018
Looking back on it, I just
want to prove people wrong.

00:00:14.120 --> 00:00:16.629
I just go out there, I grab the ball,

00:00:16.629 --> 00:00:20.046
and I think to myself, "I run this game."

00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:33.029
Growing up, my mom, my dad, they wanted

00:00:33.029 --> 00:00:34.783
me and my brother to play sports,

00:00:34.783 --> 00:00:36.343
find something that we love.

00:00:36.343 --> 00:00:39.063
I got a lot of stares
and a lot of questions

00:00:39.063 --> 00:00:41.341
but for me, I’m always just like,

00:00:41.341 --> 00:00:42.504
"Yeah, I was born with it."

00:00:42.504 --> 00:00:45.706
It's like I don't know
any other way, this is me.

00:00:45.706 --> 00:00:48.564
- Dylan has Proteus syndrome.

00:00:48.564 --> 00:00:52.731
Once a baby is born, their
body parts never stop growing.

00:00:53.656 --> 00:00:55.295
In the first five years of his life,

00:00:55.295 --> 00:00:58.095
he had six surgeries,
but Dylan's been able

00:00:58.095 --> 00:01:00.512
to deal with those and adapt.

00:01:01.455 --> 00:01:04.225
- In my case, it was my
fingers and my toes.

00:01:04.225 --> 00:01:07.025
I can't really move these three fingers

00:01:07.025 --> 00:01:08.608
and then these two.

00:01:10.025 --> 00:01:13.076
I had issues that most
people take for granted,

00:01:13.076 --> 00:01:15.114
like buttoning up a shirt.

00:01:15.114 --> 00:01:17.745
And the sleeved ones, those are the worst.

00:01:17.745 --> 00:01:19.025
- He thinks that if you can do it,

00:01:19.025 --> 00:01:22.945
he should be able to do it, and
he figures out how to do it.

00:01:22.945 --> 00:01:24.915
- [Dylan] Baseball has
always been my favorite sport

00:01:24.915 --> 00:01:26.775
but I've had some obstacles 'cause

00:01:26.775 --> 00:01:28.615
I've had to figure out how to catch,

00:01:28.615 --> 00:01:30.156
'cause I can't squeeze my glove,

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:32.385
and it's the same thing
with my curveball.

00:01:32.385 --> 00:01:35.265
Most people have both fingers on it but

00:01:35.265 --> 00:01:38.116
I just use one, and I learned a new grip.

00:01:38.116 --> 00:01:40.236
- The way the ball comes
off of his middle finger

00:01:40.236 --> 00:01:41.944
and ring finger, he just
gets a lot more spin

00:01:41.944 --> 00:01:43.454
than normal people do.

00:01:43.454 --> 00:01:45.644
- It turns out, because of my condition,

00:01:45.644 --> 00:01:49.184
I can throw a curve ball
that few other pitchers can.

00:01:49.184 --> 00:01:51.225
Even though I wasn't the fastest pitcher

00:01:51.225 --> 00:01:54.204
and I didn't have the
greatest body for pitching,

00:01:54.204 --> 00:01:56.124
I always knew that I could pitch because

00:01:56.124 --> 00:01:59.076
I was accurate and I could hit my spots.

00:01:59.076 --> 00:02:00.414
- When Dylan came here as a freshman,

00:02:00.414 --> 00:02:03.053
he was never a guy that
we thought was gonna

00:02:03.053 --> 00:02:04.813
contribute as much as he did.

00:02:04.813 --> 00:02:08.464
And almost by accident
he got his opportunity.

00:02:08.464 --> 00:02:10.152
- [Dylan] We were playing our rival school

00:02:10.152 --> 00:02:12.123
in the second game of the year,

00:02:12.123 --> 00:02:14.461
and our pitcher was struggling.

00:02:14.461 --> 00:02:16.213
- [Joe] Dylan was the
only pitcher on the bench

00:02:16.213 --> 00:02:19.072
and he threw three scoreless innings.

00:02:19.072 --> 00:02:21.742
Then we kind of knew at that
point that we had something.

00:02:21.742 --> 00:02:26.482
- After that my ERA was the
second best on the team.

00:02:26.482 --> 00:02:28.822
The highlight of the year for me was

00:02:28.822 --> 00:02:33.203
when I came two outs shy
of throwing a no-hitter.

00:02:33.203 --> 00:02:35.121
A lot of people were surprised, but

00:02:35.121 --> 00:02:37.963
I knew that I could do it and it just

00:02:37.963 --> 00:02:41.523
showed everyone that I'm a good pitcher.

00:02:41.523 --> 00:02:44.132
My family who's always loving and said,

00:02:44.132 --> 00:02:47.465
"Just be you, everything will work out."

